# Principles backend

ASP.NET Core WebAPI for the Principles habit/goal app. Flutter client lives in the sibling `flutter-frontend-of-principles` repo (this folder is nested as `backend/` in the multi-root workspace).

## Git

- Host is **GitHub only** (`origin`). Do not fetch, push, or set defaults on Bitbucket or other remotes.
- **Never commit** (or amend, stash-and-drop, or push) unless the user explicitly asks in the current request. Leave finished work uncommitted and say it is ready to commit.

## Domain

- **Users / profile** — auth, slogan, mission, road-guide flag, `LastAppOpen` (latest calendar day the app was opened on any device; max-wins via `PUT api/profile/lastappopen`; included on bootstrap/changes user DTO). `User.UpdatedAt` is the profile sync stamp (`LastModified` on bootstrap/profile = `UpdatedAt ?? CreatedAt`). Email/password signup: `GET api/account/signupcode` (rejects if email already exists); forget-password / website delete step: `GET api/account/code` (requires existing user). Both accept optional `language` (`uk`/`en`, default English), email a branded HTML+plain multipart verification message via `IEmailSender` / `VerificationEmailContent` (`HostEmail` = batsbohdan@gmail.com), and store a hashed 6-digit code in `app.EmailVerificationCodes` (15 min TTL) — the API does **not** return the code. Clients must send it on `POST api/account/authentication` (`code`) and `PUT api/account/password` (`code`). Optional `?code=` on `DELETE api/account` consumes a password-reset code (website). No `GET api/account/apikey` — `AI_API_KEY` stays server-side only.
- **Goals** — user goals (`goal` schema); archive via `IsArchived` / `ArchivingTime`, `GET api/goals/archive`, `POST api/goals/archivestatus`; sync DTOs include `IsArchived`
- **Habits** — progress, frequency, reminders, areas of life (`hbt` / `arlf`)
- **Tasks** — one-off work with schedule/reminders/repeat; checklists in `tsk.TaskSubtasks`
- **Sync** — `GET api/sync/bootstrap` for first catch-up; `GET api/sync/changes?since=` for incremental peers (returns changed entities + `Deleted*Ids` from `app.SyncDeletions`; `RequiresFullBootstrap` when `since` is missing/older than 14 days). Both include AI conversations and the same reminder lists as `GET api/reminder/all`
- **Reminders** — `GET api/reminder/all` remains for clients that only need reminders; bootstrap/changes also return `GeneralReminders` + `UserHabitReminders`
- **Tasks** — `CreatedAt` / `UpdatedAt` drive changes filtering; deletes write sync tombstones
- **Progress** — progress writes bump parent habit `UpdatedAt` so the habit appears in `/sync/changes`
- **AI** — Helper chat (`POST api/ai/chat`) via Microsoft Agent Framework `ChatClientAgent`. Replies stay short (usually 4–7 sentences, or a list of at most 3 items) and concrete: one next action, using listed goal/habit/task names. Chat messages may include `attachments` (`fileName`, `mimeType`, base64 `data`) for images and small files on the latest user turn. Structured calls (parse-task, title, recommend-habits, suggest-profile-text, recommend-goals) via `IChatClient`. Conversations CRUD under `api/ai/conversations`; `AI_API_KEY` stays server-side only
- **Silent sync push** — Flutter installs register an FCM token via `PUT api/device/push-token` (`app.UserDevices`, unique `DeviceId`; `DELETE api/device/push-token/{deviceId}` on logout). After a committed task create/update/status/delete, habit update/archive/delete, or goal create/update/archive/delete, the feature service calls `ISyncPushService.NotifyOtherDevices` with the request's `X-Device-Id` (deleted ids for task/habit deletes). `SyncPushDispatcher` (singleton hosted service) batches per user for ~2 s and sends one data-only FCM v1 message `{type: sync, deletedTaskIds, deletedHabitIds}` (APNs `background`, priority 5) to every device except the `X-Device-Id` origin (all devices when several made changes). Dead tokens are deleted. Credentials: `FIREBASE_CREDENTIALS_JSON` (raw or base64) or `FIREBASE_CREDENTIALS_PATH`, optional `FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID`; unset = pushes disabled. Never commit service-account JSON

## Client contract

- Prefer camelCase JSON DTOs in `SET.BusinessLogic/Models`
- Nested task `subtasks`: `null`/omitted = keep existing rows; empty array = clear
- Completing a subtask does **not** complete the parent task
